  "reading": "plan_a",
  "readings": {
    "F1": "q of an arm is the mean over its seeds with O-bank answers of the per-seed share of the O items whose flag differs from \u03b80's flag (equal to the share over all seed x prompt pairs, since every seed holds every item); the per-seed shares are printed. Alternative: one seed's q, or the median over seeds.",
    "F2": "P and J are the reading's own (the O items and the repair arm's O seeds): under plan A they equal the planning values P = 500, J = 6 (REV4:565); under block A only (J = 3) and plan B (J = 9) the formula takes the reading's J, and the output flags that it differs from the planning J. Alternative: P = 500 and J = 6 always.",
    "F3": "The rows are REV4's two Branch-full rows (seed SD 0 and 1.15 pp) at the measured q, with no added discordance: under Branch 128 the measured q already holds the cut's flag changes, so the +3 and +6 pp rows (planning allowances for them) are not added again. Alternative: all four rows, the Branch 128 rows at q + 0.03 and q + 0.06.",
    "F4": "The columns are REV4's two levels, 5% per comparison and 0.375% inside \u03a6, not the level F_k reached in this reading's \u03a6 run (F_k starts with weight 0; B16's level is printed beside the power). Alternative: the power at F_k's own final level.",
    "F5": "\u0394 = 0 and \u03c4_O* = 5 pp (\"an arm at \u03b80's level feasible at 5 pp\"): planning power, not observed power; the measured O estimate against \u03b80 is printed beside it, never put into the formula. Alternative: none in the text."
  },
  "rule": [
